 ] Specify how per-project context reaches preflight_status_mapping so it can classify a drift-eligible unmapped status — either thread the resolved effective map / project key into it (and update its caller reconcile.py:485) or state why the module-level canonical map suffices.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.0778,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["reconcile_helpers.py:88 `mapping = getattr(cfg, \"local_to_jira_status\", {}) or {}` — module-level, no project key","reconcile.py:485 is the sole caller `preflight_status_mapping(mutations)` passing only mutations","Plan: preflight 'no longer counts a drift-eligible unmapped status as offending' but drift-eligibility is defined by the effective (per-project) map"],"finding":"reconcile_helpers.preflight_status_mapping reads the MODULE-LEVEL dict config.local_to_jira_status (project-agnostic), but the plan requires it to treat a 'drift-eligible unmapped status as non-offending' — a determination that depends on the PER-PROJECT effective map. The plan does not enumerate how project context (project key or the resolved effective map) is delivered into preflight_status_mapping, whose sole caller is reconcile.py:485.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd03a56f07881ac74","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 3 / Scope: reconcile_helpers.py","norm_id":"n3ccdd099245bd2c9","priority":0.7778,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A status unmapped in the built-in default but present under [mapping.projects.<KEY>] (or vice-versa) is misclassified by a project-agnostic preflight"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7778,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","i