coded blocked/cancelled `_STATUS_ANNOTATION_LABEL` maps and duplicated `_REBAR_STATUS_LABEL_TO_LOCAL` literals are removed and the shared helper is the sole source (e.g. a grep/absence assertion plus the shared helper being re-exported in `applier.__all__`).","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5d","T5e"],"criteria":["E1"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"retire the duplicated `_REBAR_STATUS_LABEL_TO_LOCAL` literals they import\"","\"re-export the shared helper in `__all__` in place of the retired literal\"","E1(d): for migrations, criteria verify BOTH removal and replacement — the four ACs cover config-effect, drift, collapse round-trip, and parity, but none asserts the old literals/hardcoded maps are gone."],"finding":"The plan describes a migration — retiring the duplicated `_REBAR_STATUS_LABEL_TO_LOCAL` literals and the hardcoded blocked/cancelled `_STATUS_ANNOTATION_LABEL` maps and replacing them with the shared parse helper / derived stamp rule — but no acceptance criterion verifies the REMOVAL of the old literals (only the replacement round-trip behavior is asserted).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f348a3ac55900cfb8","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope (files): inbound_translate.py / apply_inbound_events.py / inbound_differ.py / applier.py; Acceptance Criteria","norm_id":"n482dbfdb00e4ee87","priority":1.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An implementer wires the new shared helper but leaves a stale `_REBAR_STATUS_LABEL_TO_LOCAL` literal or the hardcoded blocked/cancelled map in place; all four ACs still pass, silently leaving two sources of truth."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add an AC: \"The duplicated `_REBAR_STATUS_LABEL_TO_LOCAL` literals and hardcoded blocked/cancelled annotation maps are removed; consumers import the single shared parse helper (verified by an import/absence check and `applier.__all__` re-export).\"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"missing_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Define the stamp/label-diff behavior when `status_map[local]` is absent (drift) or equals the `SKIP` sentinel — guard the `effective_jira_to_local[status_map[local]]` lookup and state whether a drifted/SKIP status leaves existing rebar-status labels untouched or removed.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.265,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Step 3 defines drift as 'a local status ABSENT from the map', and S1 (rebar:bfe7-0900-c3d1-4141) defines `mapping_config.SKIP` = intentional drop","Step 4's stamp predicate indexes `status_map[local]` unconditionally; for a drifted local status that key is absent (KeyError), and for a SKIP entry the value is the sentinel, not a Jira workflow name to feed `effective_jira_to_local[...]`","The plan omits `status` outbound on drift (step 3) but does not say whether the rebar-status label should still be stamped/removed in that case, nor how `_diff_status_annotation_labels` guards the sentinel/absent lookup"],"finding":"The stamp rule `effective_jira_to_local[status_map[local]] != local` and its inbound counterpart are not specified for the drift case (local ABSENT from the effective map) or the S1 `SKIP` sentinel, where `status_map[local]` KeyErrors or is the SKIP sentinel rather than a Jira status.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5c89aa9b83974165","impact":0.536,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 4 (Generalised rebar-status: round-trip) / step 3 (Drift) / outbound_labels.py scope line","norm_id":"n65c272f71cb23c56","priority":0.335,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A ticket whose local status is unmapped (drift) reaches `_diff_status_annotation_labels` → indexing `status_map[local]` raises or misbehaves","A status configured as SKIP reaches the stamp predicate → sentinel fed into the reverse map"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Enumerate how the resolved status_map/project-key reaches adapters/jira/acli.transition_issue — name the intermediate acli.update_issue caller (acli.py:187) and the applier→backend threading, or clarify that the mapper already resolves the value and acli needs no change.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.3944,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["acli.py:149 `resolved = _LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA.get(status, status.replace(\"_\",\" \").title())`","acli.py:187 `transition_issue(jira_key, status)` called from update_issue","outbound_differ resolves the project key; plan threads status_map 'to the mappers' but the acli transition site is reached through applier→backend, not the mapper","Plan Scope names only acli.py, not update_issue or the applier/backend threading"],"finding":"The plan lists adapters/jira/acli.py ('transition name via effective map') as reading the effective status map, but does not enumerate the intermediate caller acli.update_issue (which invokes transition_issue at acli.py:187) nor the applier→backend call chain that must thread the resolved project key / status_map from outbound_differ down to transition_issue. transition_issue(jira_key, status) currently takes no status_map/project param and reads module-level _LOCAL_STATUS_TO_JIRA.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f6333dee9c13f6c5e","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 2 / Scope: adapters/jira/acli.py","norm_id":"n6074fbdf736907a9","priority":0.3056,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A per-project status override must change the ACLI transition target but the resolved map never reaches transition_issue because no parameter carries it through update_issue"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5556,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no"